-- title:
--   Isaacs §4B: Mann's theorem on small conjugacy classes
-- statement:
--   Formalizes Isaacs, *Finite Group Theory*, §4B (pp. 125–128): the subgroup $M(G)$ generated by the conjugacy classes of the two smallest sizes, and Mann's theorems bounding its nilpotence class. The generators are the elements whose class size is a lower bound for all nontrivial class sizes, an encoding that avoids naming $n_2$ and degenerates gracefully for abelian groups.
--
--   Main definitions: `classCard` (class size as the index of the centralizer), `mannGenerators` (the generating set of $M(G)$), `mannSubgroup` ($M(G)$) and `mannSubgroup_normal` ($M(G)\trianglelefteq G$).
